ube channel is amazing she  posts music videos as a solo artist and  she's really talented she also post  various blogs and videos that show what  her life is like she's a normal teen she  even got braces as part of her 12 days  of Christmas videos we feel your pain  Rosie Rosie also has a pretty active  Instagram account with an impressive  half a million followers the account is  managed by her mom which makes sense  because Rosie is still so young  Rosie's middle name is Grace just like  her older cousin but unlike Sophia Rosie  just prefers to go by her first name she  has released her song and music video  handstands in 2018 this was a  collaboration with producer Jordan  Richmond and songwriters Heather Miley  and Griffith Frank they're the same team  that made Jo Jo see waz song boomerang  so popular it's pretty awesome that  they're working with Rosie now handstand  is a fun and up  seong it's set on a beach and is all  about looking at life through a positive  lens it's just so rosy and now rosie has  her own hype girls we love the  choreography in the video it's such a  catchy tune  Sophia Grace Brownlee Sophia Grace has  done a lot of growing up in the last  seven years and she wants you to know it  then now 15 year old is barely  recognizable she's no longer the pink  loving tutu wearing tiny diva that stole  our hearts and she's celebrating the  change one thing has stayed the same  though and that's Sophia Grace's love of  rap while her cousin Rosie has gone for  a more pop star image Sophia Grace is  building a career as a female rapper we  don't doubt that nicki minaj's influence  has something to do with this Sophia  Grace has been rapping for years now  just like her cousin Rosie Sophia Grace  has an active presence on YouTube and  she posts a little bit of everything she  does blogs about her life and advice  videos she interviews celebrities and  does makeup tutorials and she also posts  original music videos her music videos  have changed just as much as she has her  first videos like Hollywood and best  friends had a very pop star feel to them  she still looked young and her music  felt young but she has one amazing voice  in 2017 her video why you mad  looked a lot more grown-up she followed  that up with number one in August 2000  18 her deep jazzy voice was really  unique but the first week of 2019 marked  a huge change for Sophia Grace her first  rap song dropped can't sleep starts with  Sophia Grace talking about changing  she's tired of people expecting her to  be who she has always been but  everything changes including her she  raps about people's expectations and  becoming her own person the video is  Edgar than anything she's done before  and people were shook no one can believe  this is the same kid that talked about  how great the color pink is on The Ellen  Show Sophia Grace is also crazy active  on Instagram her account is pretty much  what you would expect from a teen girl  she posts lots of mirror selfies and  photos of her makeup and her makeup is  always on point she's stylish and  travels a lot we love seeing all the  places she goes to she's posted about a  boy and later about possible heartbreak  Sophia Grace is more or less a normal  teen girl who happened  to be fairly famous and she has over 1.3  million followers on her instead camp  which is pretty impressive Sophia Grace  is a lot more than just a budding Ellen  Show star she actually cares about a lot  of issues one Instagram post highlights  International Women's Day  she even interviewed Benedict  Cumberbatch on her YouTube channel  that's right none other than Doctor  Strange himself made an appearance on  her video he talked about bullying  gender equality and plenty of other hot  issues she's still a kid at heart though  she's made slime on her Channel  she did the bean boozled challenge with  Jojo sua  she was dared to dance awkwardly in  front of strangers at VidCon it seems  that she's a lot higher than she used to  be 